      <div class="formula" id="formula"></div>
      <h3>What counts as pre-token</h3>
      <p>A protocol is ranked only when its snapshot record carries no token (no market cap, no CoinGecko id, no symbol) <em>and</em> it is not a wrapped, staked or bridged product of one that trades: its category is not Bridge, Canonical Bridge, Liquid Staking, Liquid Restaking, Restaked BTC or CEX; its name carries no whole word <em>wrapped</em>, <em>staked</em> or <em>staking</em>; it does not begin with an exchange's name; and its name ends in no version marker.</p>
      <h3>What the numbers do not say</h3>
      <p>An implied value is this entry's own claim about what a launch would be worth if the protocol's record stayed as it is. It does not predict whether or when a token is issued. A protocol "records no token" in the snapshot; that is not proof it has none.</p>
      <h3>Farm plans</h3>
      <p>Each plan is derived from the protocol's own record — its category, its chains, its TVL and its age — and states what each step costs and how long it takes. Never pay to claim: a real claim link comes from the protocol's own page.</p>
